WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:17.189 align:start position:0%
 
she  my name is lina khalifa  i'm the owner and founder of shifter the  first self-defense studio for women in  the middle east  i teach a mix between  taekwondo boxing  and pure self-defense techniques  we also empower women through seminars  and workshops like domestic violence  sexual harassment assaults and also  women empowerment  i started in 2004 because one of my  friends got abused  by her father and brothers i was really  upset about her situation because i have  a background in martial arts i decided  to start giving lessons for women in  self-defense  domestic violence is the high percent in  jordan in in violence for women  we have street harassment you don't see  lots of girls walking the street because  of that  shifter is safe place for women to come  and talk about their issues because  all the other girls have been mostly the  same experience  the physical training and mental  training both are really important so we  start with talking to the girls about  their stories  then we move to the training  we have trained and empowered more than  12 000 women  before i joined i was facing like a lot  of verbal harassment i felt so weak  because i couldn't do anything about it  since i joined verbal harassment is less  now because i'm more confident now so  when walking in street that shows like  that reflects to other people  most girls here after the training they  feel that  they can't stand up for themselves  it's about providing them with  self-defense skills to defend their  rights and to have a voice in society  you

